          <div class="info-content">
            <section id="get-in-touch" aria-labelledby="get-in-touch-title">
              <span class="info-number" aria-hidden="true">01 / 04</span>
              <h2 id="get-in-touch-title">Talk to a person.</h2>
              <p>For help, email <a href="mailto:google@remej.dev">google@remej.dev</a>. Support is handled by Reme Le Hane in South Africa. Include your app version, iOS version, what you tried, and any warning text that does not contain personal information.</p>
              <div class="info-callout"><strong>Keep your data private.</strong> Do not email your Instagram export, usernames, passwords, receipts, or relationship lists. They are not needed to start a support request.</div>
            </section>

            <section id="import-help" aria-labelledby="import-help-title">
              <span class="info-number" aria-hidden="true">02 / 04</span>
              <h2 id="import-help-title">Trouble importing?</h2>
              <p>Select an official Instagram export rather than screenshots or a copy of your profile page. Check the app's import preview for supported files, warnings, and whether followers and following were both included. Export formats may change; an unsupported or incomplete file may not import as expected.</p>
              <p>Review coverage before drawing conclusions: missing or partial data does not prove someone is absent. Exports cannot establish a block, deletion, rename, or the exact time a relationship changed.</p>
            </section>

            <section id="purchase-help" aria-labelledby="purchase-help-title">
              <span class="info-number" aria-hidden="true">03 / 04</span>
              <h2 id="purchase-help-title">Looking for a purchase?</h2>
              <p>Apple handles payments; Kinship uses RevenueCat to check access. If a purchase is available in your version of the app, check that you are using the Apple Account used for the purchase and look for the in-app Restore Purchases option. Restoring depends on App Store and purchase-service availability.</p>
              <p>If you cannot find the option or access is still missing, email support with a description of the issue. Do not send a password, full receipt, or payment details by email.</p>
            </section>

            <section id="privacy-help" aria-labelledby="privacy-help-title">
              <span class="info-number" aria-hidden="true">04 / 04</span>
              <h2 id="privacy-help-title">Your data matters.</h2>
              <p>Kinship processes selected export data locally and keeps imported history on your device. App data may be included in iOS or computer backups, while Apple and RevenueCat separately handle purchase-related data. Read the <a href="../privacy/">privacy page</a> for details, or email <a href="mailto:google@remej.dev">google@remej.dev</a> with privacy or deletion questions.</p>
            </section>
          </div>
